{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7e6c180701c83608","name":"card_event_embargo","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Allegiance/events/card_event_embargo","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EMBARGO","text":"The enemy gets 2 fewer kredits next turn.","flavorText":"When Japan invaded French Indochina in 1940, the United States decided to embargo all oil exports to Japan. Later, due to increased Japanese hostilities in the Pacific, the war against China, and the Japanese alliance with Germany and Italy, the United States also froze Japanese assets in America. They also embargoed scrap-metal shipments to Japan and closed the Panama Canal to Japanese shipping. These actions hit the Japanese economy hard since 80% of their oil imports and 74% of scrap-metal imports came from the United States. In answer to this the Japanese decided to attack Pearl Harbor. Japan’s leaders at the time were confident that an attack on Pearl Harbor would force the United States to negotiate a compromise and lift the heavy sanctions, rather than fight the long and bloody war that later came.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_embargo","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_embargo_title","SourceString":"EMBARGO","LocalizedString":"EMBARGO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_embargo_text","SourceString":"The enemy gets 2 fewer kredits next turn.","LocalizedString":"The enemy gets 2 fewer kredits next turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_embargo_history","SourceString":"When Japan invaded French Indochina in 1940, the United States decided to embargo all oil exports to Japan. Later, due to increased Japanese hostilities in the Pacific, the war against China, and the Japanese alliance with Germany and Italy, the United States also froze Japanese assets in America. They also embargoed scrap-metal shipments to Japan and closed the Panama Canal to Japanese shipping. These actions hit the Japanese economy hard since 80% of their oil imports and 74% of scrap-metal imports came from the United States. In answer to this the Japanese decided to attack Pearl Harbor. Japan’s leaders at the time were confident that an attack on Pearl Harbor would force the United States to negotiate a compromise and lift the heavy sanctions, rather than fight the long and bloody war that later came.","LocalizedString":"When Japan invaded French Indochina in 1940, the United States decided to embargo all oil exports to Japan. Later, due to increased Japanese hostilities in the Pacific, the war against China, and the Japanese alliance with Germany and Italy, the United States also froze Japanese assets in America. They also embargoed scrap-metal shipments to Japan and closed the Panama Canal to Japanese shipping. These actions hit the Japanese economy hard since 80% of their oil imports and 74% of scrap-metal imports came from the United States. In answer to this the Japanese decided to attack Pearl Harbor. Japan’s leaders at the time were confident that an attack on Pearl Harbor would force the United States to negotiate a compromise and lift the heavy sanctions, rather than fight the long and bloody war that later came."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'TACTICAL_AIRSTRIKE_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/TACTICAL_AIRSTRIKE_17.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_order8.t_order8","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/EMBARGO.EMBARGO","SubPathString"